From 1a836e5c870e643b72525d5cf667b849a932da3a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:50:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-48: toolbox like WinForms / WPF -- pick the tool,
 then click (or draw a box) on the surface (0.48.0)

A click on a toolbox item now picks the tool: the design surface shows a
crosshair (a shield over the page, the hint line says what to do); a click
puts the new component there, a drag puts it there with that size; Esc or a
right-click gives up. A quick second click on the same item adds it at once,
as a click did before (WinForms: double-click).
- probe: place mode -- the id'd elements under the point, innermost first
  and the form last, each with the point in its own child coordinates (a
  GroupBox's div.cli counts); a generated tab sheet (no id) is marked
- host: toolboxArm (the double-click by timing), cmdPlace (the first
  container under the point: Panel / GroupBox / the form; a button there ->
  its Panel; a tab sheet is refused with the way that works); cmdAdd takes
  { into, x, y, w, h }; the templates take a size
- README: the toolbox section; the stale "no copy / paste / delete yet"
  line replaced

Tests: lib (templates with / without a size), probe (a drag from the Save
button: button > its panel (the point in the panel's px) > form, 40x20; a
click = no size; Esc = placeCancel; nothing written, nothing selected),
smoke (a click arms; put down over spbSave -> into Panel2 at 57,11, 40x20;
a tab sheet refused; a quick second click adds at once), real VS Code (the
probe holds the tool; put down into Panel2 at 400,10, 60x24, drawn there,
ONE undo).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
